    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0788" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.73/488</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic">December 30,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letters of December 11 and December 16, 1920,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d586-f1"/> relative to 205 nautical miles of cable belonging to the
                    Western Union Telegraph Company, which were reported to be on board the cable
                    ship <hi rendition="#italic">Stephan.</hi></p>
                <p>I take pleasure in informing you that information has now been received that the
                    cable ship <hi rendition="#italic">Stephan</hi> will not now carry the cable in
                    question.</p>
                <p>With reference to the last paragraph of this Department’s letter of December 11,
                    1920, I have the honor to state that the President on December 11, 1920, signed
                    a permit authorizing the Cuban-American Telephone and Telegraph Company to lay,
                    land, maintain and operate three telegraph-telephone-submarine cables at Key
                    West Florida, connecting Key West with Habana, Cuba. As it is expected that the
                    cable ship <hi rendition="#italic">Stephan</hi> will lay this cable it is
                    suggested that you may consider it desirable to bring this information <pb
                        facs="0789" n="699" xml:id="pg699"/> to the attention of the Naval Officer
                    in charge of operations at Key West so that this cable can be laid without any
                    interference.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman H. Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
